# Optional: for app-sent emails via Resend SDK (not required for Auth confirmations)
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxx

# Auth (Supabase Dashboard):
# 1. Run migrations:
#    supabase/migrations/007_user_owned_events.sql
#    supabase/migrations/008_user_owned_academies.sql
#    supabase/migrations/009_academy_social_links.sql
#    supabase/migrations/010_event_end_date.sql
# 2. Authentication → Sign In / Providers → Email:
#    - Enabled
#    - Confirm email: ON (required — otherwise signup logs users in immediately)
#    - Google: Client ID/Secret
# 3. Google Cloud redirect URI (NOT your site):
#    https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
# 4. Authentication → URL Configuration (critical for Google redirect):
#    Site URL: https://wolnamata.pl
#    Redirect URLs (add ALL of these):
#      https://wolnamata.pl/auth/callback
#      https://wolnamata.pl/**
#      http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#      http://localhost:3000/**
#
# 5. Resend → send Auth emails (confirmation, reset password):
#    Resend: create API key at https://resend.com/api-keys
#    Supabase → Authentication → Emails → SMTP Settings → Enable Custom SMTP:
#      Sender email: noreply@wolnamata.pl
#      Sender name: wolnamata
#      Host: smtp.resend.com
#      Port: 465
#      Username: resend
#      Password: <your Resend API key>
#    Docs: https://resend.com/docs/send-with-supabase-smtp
#    Also raise Auth rate limits if needed (default ~30 emails/hour).
